
# The graphics handles: opaque wrappers around the platform's GPU objects (a WebGPU/WebGL surface, shader, program, and
# buffer in the browser, or empty records on the server). The uniform graphics API and apps only ever pass these
# handles around, never a host primitive. Mirrors the `view` handle in ../dom/view.

form surface
  link handle, mark private

form shader
  link handle, mark private

form program
  link handle, mark private

form gpu-buffer
  link handle, mark private

# Which stage a shader runs at. A union, never a stringly-typed option (see conventions).
form shader-kind
  case vertex
  case fragment

# Which primitive a draw assembles its vertices into. A union, mapped to the GL constant by the native impl.
form primitive-kind
  case triangles
  case lines
  case points
